.TH celers 1  "celers 0.3.1" 
.SH NAME
celers \- CeleRS \- Distributed task queue management CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcelers\fR [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-sink\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
CeleRS \- Distributed task queue management CLI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Log level for the CLI (error, warn, info, debug, trace).

Takes precedence over the `RUST_LOG` environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Log output format: `text` (human\-readable) or `json` (newline\-delimited JSON)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: Human\-readable text: no target, no level tag (the CLI\*(Aqs historical default output)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Newline\-delimited JSON, one object per log event
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-sink\fR \fI<SINK>\fR [default: stdout]
Log destination: `stdout` (default), `file:<path>`, or `tcp:<host:port>`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
